[
  {
    "t0": 0,
    "t1": 1.7778,
    "text": "Do you know why, in English,"
  },
  {
    "t0": 1.7778,
    "t1": 4.0,
    "text": "we sometimes use A, and sometimes THE?"
  },
  {
    "t0": 4,
    "t1": 7.0,
    "text": "For the answer, let\u2019s visit England a thousand years ago!"
  },
  {
    "t0": 7,
    "t1": 8.7778,
    "text": "In 1066, the king of England"
  },
  {
    "t0": 8.7778,
    "t1": 11.0,
    "text": "dies without an heir."
  },
  {
    "t0": 11,
    "t1": 13.5455,
    "text": "Now England needs a king:"
  },
  {
    "t0": 13.5455,
    "t1": 15.0,
    "text": "England needs a king."
  },
  {
    "t0": 15,
    "t1": 16.6364,
    "text": "But there\u2019s a problem: three men"
  },
  {
    "t0": 16.6364,
    "t1": 18.0,
    "text": "each want the throne!"
  },
  {
    "t0": 18,
    "t1": 21.0,
    "text": "First, Harold is crowned."
  },
  {
    "t0": 21,
    "t1": 24.0,
    "text": "But the king of Norway invades!"
  },
  {
    "t0": 24,
    "t1": 25.3333,
    "text": "Harold defeats him,"
  },
  {
    "t0": 25.3333,
    "t1": 28.0,
    "text": "but before he can catch his breath,"
  },
  {
    "t0": 28,
    "t1": 32.0,
    "text": "William arrives with another army!"
  },
  {
    "t0": 32,
    "t1": 33.875,
    "text": "This time, Harold is killed"
  },
  {
    "t0": 33.875,
    "t1": 35.0,
    "text": "and William becomes:"
  },
  {
    "t0": 35,
    "t1": 39.0,
    "text": "The king of England!"
  },
  {
    "t0": 39,
    "t1": 40.5,
    "text": "Notice? First we said A KING:"
  },
  {
    "t0": 40.5,
    "t1": 42.0,
    "text": "a king\u2014we haven\u2019t specified which one."
  },
  {
    "t0": 42,
    "t1": 45.0,
    "text": "But THE KING means that particular king!"
  },
  {
    "t0": 45,
    "t1": 46.3333,
    "text": "Interestingly, the roots of this distinction"
  },
  {
    "t0": 46.3333,
    "t1": 47.2222,
    "text": "go back to Old English!"
  },
  {
    "t0": 47.2222,
    "t1": 49.0,
    "text": "A comes from \u0100N, meaning \u201cone.\u201d"
  },
  {
    "t0": 49,
    "t1": 51.6923,
    "text": "THE belongs to the demonstrative family, like \u201cthat\u201d:"
  },
  {
    "t0": 51.6923,
    "t1": 54.0,
    "text": "something like \u201cthat one\u201d or \u201cthe very one.\u201d"
  },
  {
    "t0": 54,
    "t1": 55.5,
    "text": "So what\u2019s the key difference?"
  },
  {
    "t0": 55.5,
    "t1": 58.875,
    "text": "When your listener can identify exactly which thing you mean,"
  },
  {
    "t0": 58.875,
    "t1": 60.0,
    "text": "we usually use THE;"
  },
  {
    "t0": 60,
    "t1": 64.0,
    "text": "even if it hasn\u2019t been mentioned before!"
  },
  {
    "t0": 64,
    "t1": 65.5385,
    "text": "To practise this distinction,"
  },
  {
    "t0": 65.5385,
    "t1": 69.0,
    "text": "we\u2019ve prepared a visual challenge and a practical worksheet."
  },
  {
    "t0": 69,
    "t1": 71.34,
    "text": "Just comment THE"
  },
  {
    "t0": 71.34,
    "t1": 72.744,
    "text": "and we\u2019ll send them to you!"
  }
]